WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:22.566 --> 00:00:24.901
-Hey, babe.
-Hi, babe.

2
00:00:32.284 --> 00:00:33.493
Morning.

3
00:00:33.577 --> 00:00:34.578
Morning.

4
00:00:40.292 --> 00:00:41.334
Hey.

5
00:00:41.418 --> 00:00:42.419
Hey.

6
00:00:53.221 --> 00:00:54.431
-Bye.
-Bye.

7
00:01:00.353 --> 00:01:03.440
Oi! You're not going to your office?

8
00:01:04.815 --> 00:01:09.321
No. I was just gonna go to the café
and get a cup of tea first.

9
00:01:09.404 --> 00:01:10.572
Cool.

10
00:01:11.781 --> 00:01:12.949
Can I come?

11
00:01:13.617 --> 00:01:15.076
Yeah, course.

12
00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:16.161
Sweet.

13
00:01:39.976 --> 00:01:41.478
That's right.

14
00:01:41.561 --> 00:01:45.690
Make another useless policy you're gonna
backtrack on in a week. Idiots.

15
00:01:45.774 --> 00:01:47.776
Talking to the newspapers again,
sweetheart?

16
00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:49.986
Let me know if they ever talk back.

17
00:01:51.571 --> 00:01:53.365
Hello, hello. Hey, Mom.

18
00:01:53.448 --> 00:01:55.367
-Hi, darling.
-Got you these. There you go.

19
00:01:55.867 --> 00:01:57.494
Thank you. What's the occasion?

20
00:01:57.577 --> 00:01:59.788
Nothing. You know, just an ordinary day.

21
00:02:01.915 --> 00:02:02.916
Hey.

22
00:02:04.376 --> 00:02:05.377
Look at that.

23
00:02:07.796 --> 00:02:09.046
That's a good one, that.

24
00:02:14.553 --> 00:02:15.554
Hey, Dad.

25
00:02:15.637 --> 00:02:16.888
Nathan.

26
00:02:25.313 --> 00:02:26.481
Would you look at that.

27
00:02:27.691 --> 00:02:30.569
They'll let anyone in the newspapers
nowadays, won't they?

28
00:02:32.821 --> 00:02:35.615
They say humility
is not thinking less of yourself

29
00:02:35.699 --> 00:02:37.826
but thinking about yourself less.

30
00:02:39.286 --> 00:02:41.913
My little boy wonder.

31
00:02:42.914 --> 00:02:44.916
Yeah, sorry, Mom, but it's Wonder Kid.

32
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:49.129
Wunderkind, actually,
is what I think I said.

33
00:02:49.212 --> 00:02:52.257
But I just… didn't…

34
00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.541
-Hey, Doc.
-Hi, Ted. Come in.

35
00:03:26.625 --> 00:03:29.252
Yeah, okay. I wanted to thank you again

36
00:03:29.336 --> 00:03:32.005
for helping me out with that little hiccup
the other night.

37
00:03:32.088 --> 00:03:35.634
I'm actually feeling better, so I don't
know if this is necessary, really.

38
00:03:35.717 --> 00:03:37.219
Make yourself comfortable.

39
00:03:38.053 --> 00:03:39.054
Okay.

40
00:03:40.388 --> 00:03:42.891
Let me sit. I can sit here.

41
00:03:44.351 --> 00:03:45.560
It's noisy.

42
00:03:46.311 --> 00:03:49.147
Yes. You know what?
Hey, I'll, you know, go on the couch.

43
00:03:49.231 --> 00:03:50.607
Here we go. How about that?

44
00:03:51.691 --> 00:03:53.235
Hey, who am I?

45
00:03:54.277 --> 00:03:55.278
Don Draper, right?

46
00:03:56.655 --> 00:04:00.367
Yeah. Isn't that a little formal?
I don't wanna put my shoes on there.

47
00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:03.245
You know what? I'll lay down, right?
Here we go.

48
00:04:03.328 --> 00:04:07.499
I'll just pop my feet up here.
Like this, you know?

49
00:04:07.582 --> 00:04:10.627
Like a couple kids
on their top bunk on camp--

50
00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:12.712
I don't know what to do with my arm.
It feels…

51
00:04:12.796 --> 00:04:15.549
Here. Here we go. This is what we'll do.

52
00:04:15.632 --> 00:04:19.844
We'll go just classic, how you see,
like, in New Yorker cartoons.

53
00:04:19.928 --> 00:04:21.555
Right? Know what?

54
00:04:21.638 --> 00:04:24.641
I'll put this under here
to help even out my spine.

55
00:04:24.724 --> 00:04:26.893
Then-- Yeah, that feels nice. Okay.

56
00:04:26.977 --> 00:04:29.854
Now, what do I do here? Do I just--
No, that's like…

57
00:04:31.648 --> 00:04:34.859
Like I'm going down a water slide
or something like that. Like a luge.

58
00:04:35.777 --> 00:04:38.780
That's a little too "casket-y,"
isn't it? Okay.

59
00:04:38.863 --> 00:04:40.740
How about-- Here, let's do this.

60
00:04:41.324 --> 00:04:43.118
All right, how's this? This good?

61
00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:45.662
Probably sitting is best.

62
00:04:46.454 --> 00:04:49.249
Sure. That's good. Okay.

63
00:04:50.083 --> 00:04:51.084
All right.

64
00:04:52.961 --> 00:04:56.214
Yeah, there we go. There you are.

65
00:04:57.382 --> 00:05:00.343
Quite intimate here, you know?
Close. Close quarters.

66
00:05:00.427 --> 00:05:03.096
It's like we're on a episode
of The Sopranos,

67
00:05:03.179 --> 00:05:06.182
without all the gratuitous violence,
which is a good thing.

68
00:05:06.266 --> 00:05:09.185
But a lot less spaghetti and clams too,
which is a bad thing.

69
00:05:09.269 --> 00:05:10.270
So…

70
00:05:10.896 --> 00:05:14.107
Hey, who's this guy? What's his story?

71
00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:17.027
You good, buddy? Yeah? Okay, good.

72
00:05:19.195 --> 00:05:22.198
Very agreeable fella, you know?
Just doin' his thing.

73
00:05:22.282 --> 00:05:25.118
-You got tissues over there, huh?
-Yes, tissues.

74
00:05:25.201 --> 00:05:26.828
Yeah. What are those for?

75
00:05:26.912 --> 00:05:29.414
Sometimes it gets a bit emotional in here.

76
00:05:30.916 --> 00:05:33.668
-Not always, but sometimes.
-Yep, yep, yep.

77
00:05:33.752 --> 00:05:35.337
Sometimes people just sneeze.

78
00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:37.797
Yeah. Yeah, they do.
Well, we both agree with you.

79
00:05:39.507 --> 00:05:42.427
Yeah. Yeah,
my hay fever's been pretty good over here.

80
00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:45.555
Must be a low pollen count in the UK, so…

81
00:05:48.391 --> 00:05:51.978
Okay. All right. Well, when do we start?

82
00:05:52.729 --> 00:05:53.813
We've already started.

83
00:05:54.898 --> 00:05:58.485
-We started when you entered in here.
-What? Shoot!

84
00:05:58.568 --> 00:06:01.571
Well, I'm sorry. I feel like I've wasted
a bunch of time already,

85
00:06:01.655 --> 00:06:05.325
with all of the couch shenanigans
and noticing your accoutrements.

86
00:06:05.408 --> 00:06:06.952
-It's--
-Ted.

87
00:06:07.035 --> 00:06:08.036
Yeah?

88
00:06:08.745 --> 00:06:10.121
Don't worry.

89
00:06:12.624 --> 00:06:14.626
Yeah. No, of course.
I'm not worried at all.

90
00:06:14.709 --> 00:06:15.710
Yeah.

91
00:06:18.213 --> 00:06:19.214
Okay.

92
00:06:36.273 --> 00:06:38.275
What-- I mean,
what do you wanna talk about?

93
00:06:39.317 --> 00:06:42.195
Why don't you tell me
what happened the other night?

94
00:06:42.279 --> 00:06:43.697
Yeah. I don't wanna do this.

95
00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:02.883
All right, come on! Come here,
come here, come here, come here.

96
00:07:02.966 --> 00:07:03.967
All right, fellas.

97
00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:07.596
Look, there are two things you can't
ever let the other team know, all right?

98
00:07:07.679 --> 00:07:09.806
The first one's your home address.
Mark my words.

99
00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:13.518
You'll start having food deliveries
and SWAT teams showing up 24-7,

100
00:07:13.602 --> 00:07:15.145
which is nuts, 'cause in my day,

101
00:07:15.228 --> 00:07:17.355
all we had to worry about
was crank phone calls.

102
00:07:17.439 --> 00:07:21.276
Then, with the advent of caller ID,
that joy got 86'd from the prank menu,

103
00:07:21.359 --> 00:07:24.487
which is a darn shame, 'cause
the Jerky Boys were a national treasure.

104
00:07:24.571 --> 00:07:26.281
Y'all should give them a google sometime.

105
00:07:27.073 --> 00:07:28.074
But I digress.

106
00:07:28.158 --> 00:07:31.494
The second thing that you don't want your
opponent to know is that you're tired.

107
00:07:31.578 --> 00:07:34.122
Okay, look, I know y'all are exhausted.
I get it.

108
00:07:34.205 --> 00:07:35.832
But I don't want you to show it.

109
00:07:35.916 --> 00:07:38.793
I don't wanna see y'all walking around
with your tired faces, all…

110
00:07:42.672 --> 00:07:45.884
Okay? Just huffing and puffing
around the pitch. Uh-uh. No, thank you.

111
00:07:45.967 --> 00:07:47.719
The only face I wanna see
from y'all is, what, Coach?

112
00:07:47.802 --> 00:07:50.639
-Game face, baby!
-Darn tootin', Vladimir Putin. Right.

113
00:07:50.722 --> 00:07:52.849
-Y'all feel me?
-Yes, Coach!

114
00:07:52.933 --> 00:07:54.726
Good. Okay, good. Now, hop up there.

115
00:07:54.809 --> 00:07:58.438
Okay. Offense, y'all gonna stick
around here with Coach Nate and Beard.

116
00:07:58.521 --> 00:08:00.440
Defense, you're coming with me and Roy.
On the hop.

117
00:08:00.523 --> 00:08:01.733
Move it!

118
00:08:04.277 --> 00:08:06.780
Okay. Right.

119
00:08:06.863 --> 00:08:09.616
Coach Nate, I hope you're not
too great to train us now.

120
00:08:09.699 --> 00:08:11.368
Thank you, Dani. Thank you.

121
00:08:11.451 --> 00:08:13.828
Those drills better be lit.
You've got a reputation to keep up.

122
00:08:13.912 --> 00:08:16.414
Yes, very funny. Thank you, Jamie.

123
00:08:16.498 --> 00:08:19.292
Lucky us. We get to be trained
by the Wonder Kid himself.

124
00:08:20.252 --> 00:08:21.253
Big man.

125
00:08:21.336 --> 00:08:24.714
Very funny, Colin.
You a stand-up comic now?

126
00:08:24.798 --> 00:08:27.842
Kind of ironic, 'cause I sat you down
at the match the other day.

127
00:08:29.844 --> 00:08:33.056
Right. I need all our best goal scorers
on the pitch right now. Go.

128
00:08:34.224 --> 00:08:37.310
Colin, Colin.
You can sit this one out, okay?

129
00:08:41.981 --> 00:08:44.317
I am a strong and capable man.

130
00:08:44.401 --> 00:08:46.486
I am a strong and capable man.

131
00:08:48.071 --> 00:08:49.698
That's my mantra.

132
00:08:50.782 --> 00:08:51.950
Cool.

133
00:09:02.627 --> 00:09:04.421
Bro, it's been two days. Still nothing?

134
00:09:04.504 --> 00:09:06.339
-No.
-Ouch, man.

135
00:09:06.423 --> 00:09:08.967
Sometimes three dots appear,
but then they go away again.

136
00:09:09.634 --> 00:09:11.094
It's over, man. I've messed up.

137
00:09:11.177 --> 00:09:14.180
Don't be negative, amigo. There might be
a good reason she hasn't replied.

138
00:09:14.264 --> 00:09:15.932
Yeah, maybe she got hit by a bus.

139
00:09:16.725 --> 00:09:18.310
Or a train?

140
00:09:18.393 --> 00:09:20.937
It's more likely she lost interest
in the relationship.

141
00:09:21.021 --> 00:09:23.648
Maybe she went back
and saw how lame these texts are.

142
00:09:24.274 --> 00:09:25.942
"My favorite film's Ratatouille."

143
00:09:26.026 --> 00:09:27.652
Hey, listen. Okay.

144
00:09:27.736 --> 00:09:29.905
It doesn't matter.
I don't care if she doesn't--

145
00:09:30.614 --> 00:09:31.656
Three dots. Three dots.

146
00:09:36.703 --> 00:09:37.996
That's a kick in the plums.

147
00:09:38.079 --> 00:09:39.247
Next time, man.

148
00:09:44.836 --> 00:09:47.255
Oh, my God. Just answer him.
It's been two days.

149
00:09:47.339 --> 00:09:49.257
I don't know what to say.

150
00:09:49.341 --> 00:09:50.342
How about the truth?

151
00:09:51.593 --> 00:09:52.594
"I'd love to meet up,

152
00:09:52.677 --> 00:09:56.640
but I'm worried that you can't live up
to the fantasy I've created in my head.

153
00:09:56.723 --> 00:09:58.725
So I'm going to let my insecurities

154
00:09:58.808 --> 00:10:02.229
keep me from possibly finding
my one true love."

155
00:10:03.563 --> 00:10:07.234
His favorite film is Ratatouille.
That's worrying, right?

156
00:10:07.317 --> 00:10:08.902
Meet him.

157
00:10:08.985 --> 00:10:11.363
Who fucking cares
what his favorite movie is?

158
00:10:11.446 --> 00:10:14.074
Also, Ratatouille
is a goddamn masterpiece.

159
00:10:14.157 --> 00:10:17.577
Ironically, it's about snobbery and how
good art can come from anywhere.

160
00:10:17.661 --> 00:10:19.746
Stop your dithering
and go fuck your cartoon rat.

161
00:10:19.829 --> 00:10:22.666
All right. Well, what if we meet up
and it all goes wrong?

162
00:10:24.417 --> 00:10:28.088
I mean, everything always goes wrong.
All relationships are a nightmare.

163
00:10:28.171 --> 00:10:32.175
My relationship is the oxygen
that gives me life.

164
00:10:32.259 --> 00:10:35.887
Apart from Leslie's marriage, which is
a bloody greeting card of some kind.

165
00:10:37.055 --> 00:10:40.892
And you and Roy are just
aggravatingly perfect in every way.

166
00:10:41.977 --> 00:10:42.978
Thank you.

167
00:10:45.063 --> 00:10:46.147
I don't know.

168
00:10:47.148 --> 00:10:49.442
It was definitely easier
when we didn't work together.

169
00:10:50.151 --> 00:10:52.821
I just feel like we're around each other
all the time.

170
00:10:52.904 --> 00:10:55.865
Wherever I go, he's my shadow.
My adorably hairy shadow, but--

171
00:11:00.787 --> 00:11:03.331
What's going on?
Why are you jazz scatting?

172
00:11:05.584 --> 00:11:06.793
Were you talking about me?

173
00:11:06.877 --> 00:11:08.795
-Yeah, we were talking about you.
-No.

174
00:11:16.636 --> 00:11:19.347
-Big whoop. You ready to go?
-Yeah.

175
00:11:20.807 --> 00:11:22.350
Answer him.

176
00:11:23.268 --> 00:11:25.353
-Bye.
-Bye.

177
00:11:29.065 --> 00:11:30.734
Two, three, four.

178
00:11:41.703 --> 00:11:43.955
-Hello.
-Hello.

179
00:11:44.039 --> 00:11:46.374
-You nearly done?
-God, no.

180
00:11:46.458 --> 00:11:48.793
To-do list's as long as my arm.

181
00:11:48.877 --> 00:11:51.338
What? This arm?

182
00:11:55.258 --> 00:11:56.801
Maybe.

183
00:11:57.886 --> 00:11:59.262
Oi, that's not helping me.

184
00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:02.349
All right. I'll give you your arm back.

185
00:12:02.432 --> 00:12:03.558
Thank you.

186
00:12:03.642 --> 00:12:05.644
I'll take your neck.

187
00:12:12.692 --> 00:12:15.528
Seriously, I have got a lot of work to do.

188
00:12:15.612 --> 00:12:17.906
So if you're gonna be here,
you need to go sit quietly on the couch

189
00:12:17.989 --> 00:12:19.324
and read your book, yeah?

190
00:12:22.619 --> 00:12:23.995
Thank you.

191
00:12:44.641 --> 00:12:46.142
That's not helping me either.

192
00:12:46.226 --> 00:12:50.063
What? I'm doing exactly what you said.
I'm sitting quietly and reading my book.

193
00:12:50.146 --> 00:12:54.359
You doing exactly what I tell you to do
is so fucking hot.

194
00:13:13.837 --> 00:13:16.089
-Hello, Ted.
-What's up, Doc?

195
00:13:16.715 --> 00:13:18.258
I'm surprised you came back.

196
00:13:18.341 --> 00:13:19.968
Yeah, well, I don't quit things.

197
00:13:29.519 --> 00:13:32.606
-How are you, Ted?
-I'm swell, as well as fine and dandy.

198
00:13:32.689 --> 00:13:34.524
-How about you, Doc?
-I'm well.

199
00:13:34.608 --> 00:13:35.609
Glad to hear it.

200
00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:39.571
So, is this your first time doing therapy?

201
00:13:39.654 --> 00:13:43.283
No, ma'am. My wife and I did
couple's therapy for a little while.

202
00:13:44.492 --> 00:13:45.493
How was that?

203
00:13:45.577 --> 00:13:46.870
Well, let's see.

204
00:13:47.454 --> 00:13:50.081
I'm here in London,
and my wife is back in Kansas,

205
00:13:50.165 --> 00:13:53.126
which is a good thing 'cause if she heard
me referring to her as my wife still,

206
00:13:53.209 --> 00:13:54.628
she'd be hopping mad.

207
00:13:54.711 --> 00:13:57.005
How long these little chats you do take?

208
00:13:57.088 --> 00:13:59.424
Sessions typically last 50 minutes.

209
00:13:59.507 --> 00:14:01.968
Okay. But you charge by the hour, right?

210
00:14:02.052 --> 00:14:03.428
That's correct.

211
00:14:09.184 --> 00:14:11.394
I take it you're not a fan
of this kind of work?

212
00:14:11.478 --> 00:14:12.771
No, ma'am.

213
00:14:12.854 --> 00:14:14.147
Why's that, do you think?

214
00:14:14.856 --> 00:14:15.899
You want the truth?

215
00:14:15.982 --> 00:14:18.568
I'm only interested in the truth, Ted.

216
00:14:20.904 --> 00:14:22.197
'Cause I think it's bullshit.

217
00:14:23.823 --> 00:14:27.035
You don't know me. We don't have history.

218
00:14:27.118 --> 00:14:29.079
And yet you just expect me
to spill my guts

219
00:14:29.162 --> 00:14:31.498
about all the gory details of my life.

220
00:14:32.082 --> 00:14:34.918
The fights, the mistakes,
my deep dark secrets.

221
00:14:35.544 --> 00:14:37.963
But you ain't listening
'cause you care about me.

222
00:14:38.046 --> 00:14:42.217
No. No, you're only listening to me
'cause you're paid to listen to me.

223
00:14:43.677 --> 00:14:47.430
You're getting paid to just jot down
your little notes and diagnose my tears.

224
00:14:47.514 --> 00:14:49.975
And then what?
Probably just blame it on my folks, right?

225
00:14:50.892 --> 00:14:53.645
I mean, you say you're only interested
in the truth.

226
00:14:53.728 --> 00:14:56.982
And yet here you are, charging an
hourly rate for only 50 minutes of work.

227
00:14:57.065 --> 00:14:58.316
Like I said, it's bullshit.

228
00:15:14.499 --> 00:15:15.834
-Hey.
-Nathan.

229
00:15:20.213 --> 00:15:21.423
Oh, my God.

230
00:15:21.506 --> 00:15:22.841
-Sorry.
-Sorry, Sam.

231
00:15:22.924 --> 00:15:24.217
Ms. Welton. Hi.

232
00:15:24.301 --> 00:15:26.469
-Call me Rebecca.
-Rebecca. Rebecca, sorry.

233
00:15:27.387 --> 00:15:28.430
These machines, huh?

234
00:15:28.513 --> 00:15:31.308
We've never been so connected,
yet never further apart.

235
00:15:34.686 --> 00:15:36.313
Is that what you were gonna say?

236
00:15:37.105 --> 00:15:39.190
Yes. Yes, it was.

237
00:15:41.818 --> 00:15:44.446
-All right. Have a good day.
-Right. I'll see you later.

238
00:15:44.529 --> 00:15:46.489
-You too. Bye.
-See you, Sam.

239
00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:49.701
Yes.

240
00:15:55.582 --> 00:15:58.585
Hello. Your new pens have arrived.

241
00:16:06.801 --> 00:16:08.303
I'll just leave 'em here.

242
00:16:08.386 --> 00:16:09.387
Yeah, all right.

243
00:16:10.096 --> 00:16:11.223
'Kay.

244
00:16:11.306 --> 00:16:12.599
